{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'pwd; git status --short; cat .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md; git diff 80f91a6a..79193a88 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'pwd; git status --short; cat .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md; git diff 80f91a6a..79193a88 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go'","aggregated_output":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree\n---\nname: pose-review\ndescription: Use for POSE pull-request or code review to verify controlled scope, preserved contracts, security and observability impact, risk-proportional validation, and escalation where applicable. Trigger keywords - review, code review, PR review, review opinion, ultrareview.\nwhen_to_use: Evaluating your own or another author's diff or PR under POSE. Use before commenting or approving to select rules, inspect validation evidence and prior decisions, and issue an actionable decision.\npose_schema_range: \"1-1\"\nclients: agents-skills, mcp, claude-code\ncapabilities: read\n---\n\n# Skill: pose-review\n\n## Required reading\n\n1. [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md).\n2. [`.pose/workflows/review.md`](../../../.pose/workflows/review.md).\n3. Applicable domain rules; security takes precedence in conflicts.\n\nResolve the selected task with `pose context --task <typed-or-qualified-artifact-ref> --json` before reviewing. Follow its canonical authority and stop on ambiguity, stale binding, unsupported metadata or `transfer-in-progress`. Use the qualified `xref:` scope for cross-project review; every cross-project write requires an explicit `POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS` binding and the current `context_revision` as `--expect-context`. Keep review evidence and its `POSE-Spec:` trailer in the authority repository.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Classify the change as feature, bugfix, refactor, documentation, or mixed.\n2. Run `pose assess tech-debt` during code review to ensure markers (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `stub`, `panic`) are covered by follow-ups or specs. Run `pose assess integrate` when touching inter-module contracts (Protobuf, Kafka, REST, MCP).\n3. Resolve `pose review bundle <scope> --explain` to inspect effective criteria, components and tool requirements.\n4. Run active required tools first, record why each recommended tool was used or skipped, and keep completion tools deferred until attestation.\n5. Select rules with `pose suggest review --path <affected-dir>` for every mapped component.\n6. Search `.pose/knowledge/` for prior module decisions, accepted risks, and pending follow-ups.\n7. Require deterministic `pose validate --strict` evidence matching delivery targets.\n8. Evaluate every required plan criterion, including cross-component boundaries. When the change adds or alters a governance gate, also answer: what is the cheapest way to satisfy this gate in form without producing its value, and what stops that? Point to the adversarial corpus case that proves it (`pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md`), or record the gap.\n9. Classify findings as critical, high, medium, or low with evidence and expected action.\n10. Run `pose recurrence-check --tolerant --window-days 14`; use recurrence escalation for a matching systemic signal.\n11. Create a handoff with `pose new-knowledge handoff <slug>` for accepted residual risk, monitoring, or deferred action.\n12. Seal the review subject with `pose review bundle <scope> --seal`.\n13. Prepare the mechanical half with `pose review auto-attest <bundle-id> --reviewer agent:<id>` — without `--apply` — and read `review_attestation.pending`: those are the criteria no registered check answers, and they are yours to answer. Then record the attestation with `pose review attest`, giving every judgment criterion a conclusion. `--apply` on auto-attest records only when nothing is pending; it refuses otherwise, and never answers a judgment criterion for you. An explicit attestation records `--criterion ID|passed|evidence` (or `not-applicable` with a rationale, or `finding` naming a recorded finding) and `--finding ID|severity|disposition|action|evidence[|owner|rationale|review-by]`; every finding needs a severity and an action, and an `accepted-risk` or `wont-fix` finding also needs an owner, a rationale and a review date. A `passed` criterion may cite only evidence the sealed bundle contains, of a class the criterion accepts. For a cross-project attestation, use the qualified `xref:` as the target argument to `pose review attest`, include `--expect-context <digest>` with `--apply`, and keep the explicit project binding; a bundle ID alone does not select an authority project.\n14. Run `pose review verify <scope>` and `pose review-check <scope>`; close only when both confirm a valid, approved attestation.\n15. Decide: approved, approved with reservations, changes requested, or rejected.\n16. When Contributor Mode is active, if review uncovers POSE linter false-positives, diagnostic frictions, or rule gaps, stage an improvement proposal with `pose contribute stage --type enhancement --title \"<summary>\"`.\n\n## Output requirements\n\n- Completed Rules applied during review section.\n- Bundle/plan digests and dispositions for required, recommended and deferred completion tools.\n- Severity-classified findings with expected actions.\n- Clear and actionable final decision.\n- Handoff when residual risk is accepted.\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\nindex 977f604e..848de4f0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n@@ -1420,7 +1420,14 @@ func cmdValidateWithStore(store posemodel.Store, args []string, stdout, stderr i\n \t// A check that changed a tracked file changed the material it ran over: the\n \t// committed tree no longer describes what was validated.\n \tendedClean := materialTrackedUnchanged(root)\n-\trun.MaterialClean = startedClean && endedClean\n+\t// The run validated its recorded head only if HEAD never moved: a commit\n+\t// made while checks ran would let them observe code the record does not\n+\t// name (review round 4, N10).\n+\tendHead := \"\"\n+\tif head, err := gitOutputBounded(root, 1024, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"); err == nil {\n+\t\tendHead = strings.TrimSpace(string(head))\n+\t}\n+\trun.MaterialClean = startedClean && endedClean && run.GitHead != \"\" && endHead == run.GitHead\n \tif len(run.MaterialProvenance) > 0 && !endedClean {\n \t\tfor spec := range run.MaterialProvenance {\n \t\t\trun.MaterialProvenance[spec] = posemodel.MaterialBindingUnavailable\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\nindex d93bc0f6..af0e2978 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\n@@ -104,6 +104,14 @@ func planCarry(root, resultsPath, mode, matrixSHA string, matrix validationMatri\n \tif !materialWorktreeClean(root) {\n \t\treturn unused(\"the working copy differs from HEAD in material paths\")\n \t}\n+\t// Selection is lexical: a module reached through a symlink aliases another\n+\t// path, so its inputs cannot be told apart (review round 4, N9).\n+\tfor _, module := range modules {\n+\t\tresolved, err := filepath.EvalSymlinks(module.Abs)\n+\t\tif err != nil || filepath.Clean(resolved) != filepath.Clean(module.Abs) {\n+\t\t\treturn unused(\"module %s is reached through a symlink, so its changes cannot be attributed\", module.Rel)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tif err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", base.GitHead, \"HEAD\").Run(); err != nil {\n \t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result's head %s is not an ancestor of HEAD\", base.GitHead)\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go\nindex 14f1841a..f9f05fb0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go\n@@ -463,7 +463,70 @@ func TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\n \tf.git(\"update-index\", \"--add\", \"--cacheinfo\", \"160000,\"+second+\",vendor\")\n \tf.git(\"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\", \"commit\", \"-qm\", \"move the gitlink\")\n \t_, out := runValidate(t, f.root, \"--changed-from\", \"HEAD~1\", \"--changed-to\", \"HEAD\", \"--explain\")\n-\tif !strings.Contains(out, \"+ b: root-level change outside any module: vendor\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"- a: not affected\") {\n+\tif !strings.Contains(out, \"+ b: declared dependency vendor/lib changed: vendor\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"- a: not affected\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"a gitlink above b's dependency must select b and leave a: %s\", out)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// A dependency beneath a surviving module keeps its dependents selected after\n+// it is deleted (review round 4, N7).\n+func TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := newCarryFixture(t, `{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"modules\":{\"b\":{\"selfContained\":true,\"dependsOn\":[\"a/nested\"]}}}`)\n+\tf.write(\"a/nested/go.mod\", \"module nested\\n\")\n+\tf.commit(\"nested module\")\n+\tf.baseline()\n+\tf.git(\"rm\", \"-rq\", \"a/nested\")\n+\tf.commit(\"delete the nested dependency\")\n+\t_, _, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n+\tif !strings.Contains(run.Carry.Selected[\"b\"], \"a/nested\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"selected = %v, want b selected by its deleted nested dependency\", run.Carry.Selected)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// A dependency on the project root is changed by any file once the root\n+// module is gone (review round 4, N8).\n+func TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := newCarryFixture(t, `{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"modules\":{\"a\":{\"selfContained\":true},\"b\":{\"selfContained\":true,\"dependsOn\":[\".\"]}}}`)\n+\tf.baseline()\n+\tf.write(\"root.txt\", \"edited\\n\")\n+\tf.commit(\"root change\")\n+\t_, _, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n+\tif _, ok := run.Carry.Selected[\"b\"]; !ok {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"selected = %v, want b selected through its root dependency\", run.Carry.Selected)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, ok := run.Carry.Selected[\"a\"]; ok {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"selected = %v, want a carried\", run.Carry.Selected)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// A module reached through a symlink is never carried (review round 4, N9).\n+func TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := newCarryFixture(t, \"\")\n+\tif err := os.Symlink(\"a\", filepath.Join(f.root, \"alias\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(f.root, \".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\"))\n+\tf.write(\".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\", strings.Replace(string(raw), `\"stacks\"`, `\"moduleOverrides\":{\"alias\":{\"stack\":\"go\"}},\"stacks\"`, 1))\n+\tf.commit(\"alias\")\n+\tf.baseline()\n+\tf.write(\"a/changed.go\", \"package a\\n\")\n+\tf.commit(\"change a\")\n+\t_, _, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n+\tif run.Carry == nil || run.Carry.Used || !strings.Contains(run.Carry.Reason, \"symlink\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"carry = %+v, want an aliased module refused\", run.Carry)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// A run whose HEAD moved while checks ran did not validate its recorded head\n+// (review round 4, N10).\n+func TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := newCarryFixture(t, \"\")\n+\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(f.root, \".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\"))\n+\tcommit := `git -C .. -c user.name=t -c user.email=t@t -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit -q --allow-empty -m moved`\n+\tf.write(\".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\", strings.Replace(string(raw), `\"stacks\":{\"go\":{\"checks\":[`, `\"moduleOverrides\":{\"a\":{\"checks\":[{\"name\":\"moves\",\"program\":\"sh\",\"args\":[\"-c\",\"`+commit+`\"],\"severity\":\"required\",\"evidenceClass\":\"unit\"}]}},\"stacks\":{\"go\":{\"checks\":[`, 1))\n+\tf.commit(\"a check that commits\")\n+\t_, out, run := f.validate()\n+\tif run.MaterialClean {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"material_clean = true although HEAD moved during the run: %s\", out)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex c2459867..9ac4ae18 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -140,27 +140,40 @@ func computeChangedScope(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule, ex\n \t\t}\n \t\treturn match\n \t}\n+\t// Every changed file selects, independently of one another (review rounds\n+\t// 2–4, N2, N5, N7, N8):\n+\t//   - its most specific owning module;\n+\t//   - every module under it (a gitlink or a replaced directory changes what\n+\t//     lies beneath);\n+\t//   - every module whose declared dependsOn contains it, lies under it, or\n+\t//     is the project root \".\", whether or not the dependency is discovered;\n+\t//   - when no module owns it: the root module and every module that does\n+\t//     not declare itself self-contained (safe execution wins).\n+\tselectModule := func(rel, reason string) {\n+\t\tif _, ok := sel.Selected[rel]; !ok {\n+\t\t\tsel.Selected[rel] = reason\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t// A discovered dependency reaches its dependents through the transitive\n+\t// widening below, with its own reason.\n+\tdiscovered := map[string]bool{}\n+\tfor _, m := range modules {\n+\t\tdiscovered[m.Rel] = true\n+\t}\n \tfor _, file := range sel.Changed {\n-\t\tif m := moduleOf(file); m != \"\" {\n-\t\t\tif _, ok := sel.Selected[m]; !ok {\n-\t\t\t\tsel.Selected[m] = \"contains changed file: \" + file\n+\t\towner := moduleOf(file)\n+\t\tif owner != \"\" {\n+\t\t\tselectModule(owner, \"contains changed file: \"+file)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n+\t\t\tif m.Rel != \".\" && strings.HasPrefix(m.Rel, file+\"/\") {\n+\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"changed path above the module: \"+file)\n \t\t\t}\n-\t\t} else {\n-\t\t\t// Root-level or unmapped change: safe execution wins, except for\n-\t\t\t// modules that declare their checks read nothing outside them. A\n-\t\t\t// root module owns the files no other module owns, so its\n-\t\t\t// declaration never exempts it from them (review round 2, N2). A\n-\t\t\t// declared dependency owns its paths even when it is gone from\n-\t\t\t// discovery, as after a deletion (review round 3, N5).\n-\t\t\t// A changed path above a module or a declared dependency (a\n-\t\t\t// gitlink, a replaced directory) changes everything under it.\n-\t\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n-\t\t\t\tif meta.Modules[m.Rel].SelfContained && m.Rel != \".\" && !underDeclaredDependency(file, meta.Modules[m.Rel].DependsOn) && !strings.HasPrefix(m.Rel, file+\"/\") {\n-\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n-\t\t\t\t}\n-\t\t\t\tif _, ok := sel.Selected[m.Rel]; !ok {\n-\t\t\t\t\tsel.Selected[m.Rel] = \"root-level change outside any module: \" + file\n-\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif dep, ok := declaredDependencyHit(file, meta.Modules[m.Rel].DependsOn); ok && !discovered[dep] {\n+\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"declared dependency \"+dep+\" changed: \"+file)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif owner == \"\" && (m.Rel == \".\" || !meta.Modules[m.Rel].SelfContained) {\n+\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"root-level change outside any module: \"+file)\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t}\n@@ -199,14 +212,15 @@ func firstScopeReason(reason string) string {\n \treturn reason\n }\n \n-// underDeclaredDependency reports whether file lies in one of deps, or above\n-// one of them.\n-func underDeclaredDependency(file string, deps []string) bool {\n+// declaredDependencyHit returns the declared dependency file changes: one it\n+// lies in, one it lies above, or the project root \".\", which every file\n+// changes.\n+func declaredDependencyHit(file string, deps []string) (string, bool) {\n \tfor _, dep := range deps {\n \t\tdep = filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(dep))\n-\t\tif file == dep || strings.HasPrefix(file, dep+\"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(dep, file+\"/\") {\n-\t\t\treturn true\n+\t\tif dep == \".\" || file == dep || strings.HasPrefix(file, dep+\"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(dep, file+\"/\") {\n+\t\t\treturn dep, true\n \t\t}\n \t}\n-\treturn false\n+\treturn \"\", false\n }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
