{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThree prior findings are fixed; **R3-N9 and R3-N10 remain partial**. Four blockers remain:\n\n- **N11 — high:** [validate_scope.go:172](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:172). The helper returns the first matching dependency before discovered dependencies are filtered. With modules `a`, `a/nested`, and `b`, `b.dependsOn: [\"a\", \".\"]`, and a change inside `a/nested`, the discovered `a` match masks the eligible root dependency. `b` can be carried; reversing dependency order selects it. Evaluate every eligible match.\n- **N12 — high:** [validate.go:1431](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1431). A material-changing HEAD transition clears `material_clean` but leaves the original material bindings intact. Delivery parsing ignores `material_clean`; after restoring the earlier source, those bindings can make the incorrectly attributed pass current again. Invalidate unverifiable bindings before publication.\n- **N13 — medium:** [validate_carry.go:110](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:110). `EvalSymlinks` does not identify case aliases on case-insensitive Unix filesystems. An override `A` can alias discovered module `a`, pass this guard, and retain results when `a` changes. Check physical directory identity or conservatively refuse alias reuse.\n- **N14 — high:** [validate.go:1167](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1167). HEAD is captured after carry selection. If selection finishes at H0 and HEAD advances to H1 before capture, old results can receive H1 provenance while the final head comparison passes. Capture and pin the subject before planning.\n\nThese are code-inspection findings. Additional reproduction fixtures, including a case-insensitive filesystem probe, were unavailable because scratch storage is read-only.\n\nFocused and broader tests, race tests, vet, and strict artifact-check passed. Both required matrix runs failed on sandbox write restrictions. The sealed canonical record has 236 passes; fresh required-tool validation remains unmet.\n\nApplied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N11\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 172,\n      \"summary\": \"declaredDependencyHit returns the first matching dependency before the caller filters discovered modules, masking later eligible matches. With discovered a, a/nested and b, no root module, and b.dependsOn=['a','.'], a change inside a/nested selects the nested owner; the first hit a is discarded, the root dependency is never examined, and transitive widening cannot select b. Reversing dependency order changes selection. Evaluate all eligible dependency intersections and add an order-independence regression.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N12\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1431,\n      \"summary\": \"A material-changing HEAD transition clears material_clean but does not invalidate MaterialProvenance when the ending worktree is clean. ParseDeliveryValidationRun ignores material_clean, and deliveryEvidenceCurrent accepts matching material bindings. A pass observed after a concurrent committed fix can retain bindings for the earlier failing source and become current again after that source is restored. Invalidate bindings whose observed material is unverifiable and extend the regression through delivery parsing and freshness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N13\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 110,\n      \"summary\": \"The alias guard detects symlink spelling changes but not case aliases on case-insensitive Unix filesystems. EvalSymlinks preserves ordinary component spelling there, so moduleOverrides['A'] can alias discovered module a while passing the guard. Changes recorded under a select only a, leaving an alias-specific check carried. Detect shared physical directory identity or conservatively refuse reuse for aliases; add a conditional case-insensitive-filesystem regression.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N14\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1167,\n      \"summary\": \"run.GitHead is captured after planCarry has selected checks using symbolic HEAD. If selection finishes at H0 and a concurrent commit advances HEAD to H1 before this capture, carried H0 outcomes receive H1 provenance and material_clean can remain true because the ending head also equals H1. Capture the subject before planning, use its immutable OID consistently, and invalidate evidence on drift. Add a synchronized planning-to-capture regression.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N5\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents and TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents passed. validate_scope.go:168-176 applies dependency-path handling independently of owner matching for undiscovered dependencies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N7\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:168-174 independently selects descendant modules and consumers of undiscovered dependency paths. TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents and TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N8\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:221 explicitly matches dependency '.'. TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles passed. N11 identifies a separate multiple-match ordering defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N9\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink passed and validate_carry.go:109-113 refuses symlink-reached modules. Case aliases remain undetected on case-insensitive Unix filesystems; see N13. Inspected the local Go filepath Unix implementation, which preserves non-symlink component spelling.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R3-N10\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean passed and validate.go:1430 clears material_clean for a different ending head. The producer still retains old material bindings and captures the subject after planning; see N12 and N14.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the rewritten selector and complete carry flow against R1-R10 and D1-D3, including all carried-forward findings, overlapping dependency order, nested and removed modules, root dependencies, gitlinks/submodule status handling, symlink and conditional case aliases, manifestless overrides, stack/check identity changes, criticality widening, chained origins, base eligibility, administrative exclusions, dispatch/cancellation, canonical publication guards, material provenance consumers, legacy parsing, manuals and scaffold copies. Focused and broader validation-related tests, focused race tests and vet passed. New scenarios were established by code inspection; writable scratch and case-insensitive runtime fixtures were unavailable. No separate torn-write defect was established in atomic canonical publication. Repository remained unchanged.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N14\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified the documented declaration assumptions and new guards. The implementation still assumes selection and recorded provenance observed the same HEAD, but captures that identity only after planning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N14\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused race tests passed and canonical publication remains guarded and atomic, but concurrent HEAD movement between selection and capture can produce falsely current carried evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive JSON fields, flag restrictions, legacy parsing and per-check delivery origins. Existing records retain their interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified incompatible-flag refusals, revision confinement, malformed-base fallback, metadata decoding errors and symlink fallback. Existing negative fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N12\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The producer clears material_clean while retaining bindings that the delivery parser and freshness consumer continue to accept independently of that flag.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected bounded result output, metadata errors, fallback reasons, selected-module explanations, carried counts and original observation fields. Existing diagnostic fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed additive CLI/file fields, explicit flag combinations, old-base rejection and legacy delivery fallback. No MCP signature changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N11\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing regressions pass, but equivalent dependency lists can select different checks solely because their entries are ordered differently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N11\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module reuse addresses repeated full execution, but D1 requires complete invalidation of declared inputs. First-match filtering can omit an eligible dependency even under the current R6 rules.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records original-observation reuse and the unchanged-input premise; D2 and D3 provide engine/matrix comparison and self-containment policy.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared manuals, translations, help, embedded copies, spec and ADR. They consistently describe intended carry behavior and new guards. The English embedded difference is the instance-specific Contributor Mode section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected actionable canonical-path refusals, metadata errors, symlink fallback and explain output. Existing diagnostic tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N11\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R6 requires eligible declared dependency intersections to select consumers. A preceding discovered match can suppress a later eligible match. N14 also undermines the stable-subject requirement of R2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-521f324dfd05f797\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared implementation, tests, governance and documentation changes against the spec's affected areas and artifact declarations. Changes remain within the approved carry feature.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N12\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision and output-path confinement remain intact, but unverifiable observations can retain material bindings that later satisfy delivery freshness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-521f324dfd05f797\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection and whole-matrix comparison remains smaller than per-check manifests or output caching. Evaluating all eligible dependency matches and pinning the subject are sufficient corrections within this design. The approach is invalid if dependency closure, filesystem identity or provenance cannot be established.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0 with 15 claims, 20 observations and 985 reported findings. Trailer head 87515826 differs from the sealed checkout only in delivery-integrity.json, generation.json and spec-graph.json.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used supplied sealed structural evidence and inspected the ADR and diff. Writable scratch for isolated assessment execution was unavailable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment publication would change files. Scratch creation failed with a read-only filesystem error.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment. Inspected producer, parser and material-freshness consumers directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment; no assessment output was written into the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved and consulted backend-go, security and documentation-style rules; additionally applied delivery-evidence and consumed relevant knowledge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict; it exited 1 with 236 failures because child checks could not create build directories or write caches. The committed canonical record reports 236 passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; it exited 1 with 233 failures caused by sandbox write restrictions. Independent focused and broader tests, focused race tests and vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
